{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-daily-prompt
  The theINmag Daily Prompt. A classroom-facing page a teacher opens on the
  interactive whiteboard each morning. One stunning REAL kid creation on the
  LEFT, a warm prompt panel on the RIGHT with three open discussion questions.
  Design brief: Webster. v3 iteration, 2026-09-14 (built for Webster).

  ARCHETYPE: derived from section 6.1 "Hero - story-first photo split", reworked
  so the two panes are not both photos: the creation owns the left pane (shown in
  full, never cropped or stretched) and a coloured prompt panel owns the right.
  Below the fold sits the sales loop, styled in the language of /pages/submitted:
  warm cards, a name bar with a yellow arrow, membership as the emphasised card.

  Above the fold fits ONE screen on a wide classroom display (1280px+), no scroll
  needed. On mobile the creation stacks over the prompt panel. The sales loop
  begins exactly at the fold.

  ============================ v3 changes ============================
  1. FLUID CENTRELINE, WHOLE IMAGE ALWAYS SHOWN, NEVER CROPPED. The hero is a flex
     row. The image renders at full hero height (height:100%, width:auto,
     object-fit:contain), so the art column shrink-wraps to the image's own width
     and the divide sits exactly at the image's right edge. A portrait makes a
     NARROW art column and a WIDE panel; a landscape makes a WIDE column and a
     narrower panel. The divide is driven by the image aspect, not a fixed grid.
     The column is clamped to a min-width (34% of hero) and max-width (60%); an
     image past the cap contains within it (small side or top ground, never crop).
     Full-bleed in feel: no rounded corners, no shadow, no cream mat. Any ground
     beside the image is just the day's style ground, reading as intentional space.
  2. ATTRIBUTION + WRITE-UP LIVE IN THE PANEL, OFF THE IMAGE. No on-image scrim
     credit. Above the "daily prompt" eyebrow the panel carries the creation title,
     an attribution line matching the gallery feed ("FirstName Initial. | Town STATE, age N") and the kid's own write-up
     styled as their voice. The write-up is line-clamped so a long one can never
     push the questions below the fold.
  3. THREE ROTATING COLOUR STYLES (lavender / sky / mint). Panel text stays
     inky-purple-navy everywhere, the universal safe text colour, so no pair-contrast
     rule is broken. Yellow stays rare (the membership CTA stamp only). The day's
     style derives from the entry date (epoch-day modulo 3) on "auto", stable within
     a day and cycling across days; an admin can pin a style too.
  4. DATE-DRIVEN, ONE SHUFFLE CONTROL. Each entry carries its own date. On load the
     page shows the entry with the greatest date on or before the store's current
     date, so it auto-advances each day with no edit. Earlier-dated entries form the
     past pool; a single "something different" button jumps to a RANDOM one of them,
     never re-showing the current one, disabled when the pool is empty. Future-dated
     entries are rendered hidden and are unreachable until their day arrives. Block
     order does not matter. No reload, no generation, no fold push.
  5. QUESTIONS STAY HUMAN-VISIBLE AND EDITABLE as plain block data, clearly marked
     PLACEHOLDER. Ryan and Gary see and edit every one in the theme editor before it
     displays. No live generation, ever. Appending a new day = one block on the front.
     Cadence: weekdays only; the ordered list simply holds weekday entries.

  BRAND RULES honoured: sentence case headings, no en or em dashes anywhere
  (hyphens only, code comments included), no Caveat font (Post + Inter only),
  real kid creation with a first-name + surname-initial credit matching the gallery feed, no pure-white or
  pure-yellow section backgrounds (yellow only as the CTA stamp), "theINmag"
  casing exact via the .theinmag-in span. Kid names are NOT emitted into JSON-LD
  (gallery brand-safety rule): schema stays titles + URLs only.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% render 'theinmag-character-pool' %}

<section
  class="theinmag-daily-prompt"
  data-theinmag-daily-prompt
  aria-labelledby="theinmag-daily-prompt-h1"
>
  {%- comment -%} Visually-hidden H1 carries the AEO load; the visible chrome speaks for itself. {%- endcomment -%}
  <h1 id="theinmag-daily-prompt-h1" class="theinmag-daily-prompt__vh">
    the<span class="theinmag-in">IN</span>mag daily prompt, a free classroom discussion and speaking-and-listening starter for Australian kids
  </h1>

  {%- comment -%} Polite live region so a screen reader hears which prompt is showing after navigation. {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="theinmag-daily-prompt__vh" data-dp-live aria-live="polite"></p>

  {%- comment -%}
    ===== ABOVE THE FOLD: one hero per daily entry, selected by date =====
    Every entry is a full hero (art pane + prompt panel) so its orientation class
    and colour-style class travel with it. Only the date-selected "today" entry is
    visible on load; the "something different" and "back to today's" controls toggle
    [hidden] on the past-pool entries. Future entries stay hidden. All client-side.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign total = section.blocks.size -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    DATE-DRIVEN selection. The prompt shown on load is the entry with the greatest
    date that is on or before the store's current date. Earlier-dated entries form
    the past pool ("something different" cycles through them). Future-dated entries
    are rendered hidden and are unreachable client-side until their day arrives.
    Dates compare as epoch seconds so the comparison is numeric, not string-lexical.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- assign current_index = -1 -%}
  {%- assign current_s = 0 -%}
  {%- assign earliest_index = 0 -%}
  {%- assign earliest_s = 0 -%}
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- assign b_s = block.settings.date | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- if forloop.first or b_s < earliest_s -%}
      {%- assign earliest_s = b_s -%}
      {%- assign earliest_index = forloop.index0 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if b_s <= now_s -%}
      {%- if current_index == -1 or b_s > current_s -%}
        {%- assign current_s = b_s -%}
        {%- assign current_index = forloop.index0 -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- comment -%} Everything is in the future (nothing on or before today): fall back to the earliest so the page is never blank. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if current_index == -1 -%}
    {%- assign current_index = earliest_index -%}
    {%- assign current_s = earliest_s -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%} Past-pool size: entries on or before today that are not the current one. Drives the shuffle disabled state. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign past_count = 0 -%}
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- assign b_s = block.settings.date | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- if b_s <= now_s and forloop.index0 != current_index -%}
      {%- assign past_count = past_count | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- liquid
      # Artwork source: admin image_picker first, then a theme asset (a pre-rotated
      # or otherwise hosted file in /assets/), then the entry's raw URL. The asset
      # path wins over the URL, so a sideways photo can be pre-rotated and pinned to
      # /assets/ rather than fought with a CSS transform inside the fluid divide.
      assign art_src = ''
      if block.settings.image
        assign art_src = block.settings.image | image_url: width: 1600
      elsif block.settings.image_asset != blank
        assign art_src = block.settings.image_asset | asset_url
      elsif block.settings.image_url != blank
        assign art_src = block.settings.image_url
      endif

      # Optional second image: a clean two-up in the art pane when set.
      assign art_src_2 = ''
      if block.settings.image_url_2 != blank
        assign art_src_2 = block.settings.image_url_2
      endif

      # Intrinsic size drives orientation and reserves space (no layout shift).
      assign iw = block.settings.image_w | default: 1600
      assign ih = block.settings.image_h | default: 1200
      assign orient = 'landscape'
      if ih > iw
        assign orient = 'portrait'
      endif
      # A two-up sits side by side, so it always reads as a wide (landscape) column.
      if art_src_2 != blank
        assign orient = 'landscape'
      endif

      # Role from the date-driven selection above: current (shown on load), future
      # (rendered hidden, never revealed client-side) or past (the shuffle pool).
      assign b_s = block.settings.date | date: '%s' | plus: 0
      assign is_current = false
      if forloop.index0 == current_index
        assign is_current = true
      endif
      assign dp_role = 'past'
      if is_current
        assign dp_role = 'current'
      elsif b_s > now_s
        assign dp_role = 'future'
      endif

      # Colour style: "auto" derives from the date (epoch-day modulo 3) so it is
      # stable within a day and cycles across days; an admin can pin one instead.
      assign estyle = block.settings.style
      if estyle == 'auto' or estyle == blank
        assign epochday = block.settings.date | date: '%s' | divided_by: 86400
        assign sidx = epochday | modulo: 3
        case sidx
          when 0
            assign estyle = 'lavender'
          when 1
            assign estyle = 'sky'
          else
            assign estyle = 'mint'
        endcase
      endif

      # Credit line, matching the live gallery feed format exactly:
      # "FirstName Initial. | Town STATE, age N" (e.g. "Frankie G. | Pottsville NSW, age 9").
      # State stays abbreviated (NSW / VIC / QLD / WA). Age is required and always shows.
      assign credit = block.settings.first_name | strip
      assign si = block.settings.surname_initial | strip
      if si != blank
        assign credit = credit | append: ' ' | append: si | append: '.'
      endif
      assign loc = ''
      if block.settings.town != blank
        assign loc = block.settings.town | strip
      endif
      if block.settings.state != blank
        if loc != blank
          assign loc = loc | append: ' ' | append: block.settings.state
        else
          assign loc = block.settings.state | strip
        endif
      endif
      if loc != blank
        assign credit = credit | append: ' | ' | append: loc
      endif
      if block.settings.age != blank
        assign credit = credit | append: ', age ' | append: block.settings.age
      endif

      # Human date line for the eyebrow, parsed from the ISO date on the entry.
      assign date_line = block.settings.date | date: '%A %-d %B'
    -%}

    <div
      class="theinmag-daily-prompt__hero theinmag-daily-prompt__hero--{{ estyle }} is-{{ orient }}"
      data-dp-entry
      data-dp-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
      data-dp-orient="{{ orient }}"
      data-dp-role="{{ dp_role }}"
      role="group"
      aria-roledescription="daily prompt"
      aria-label="Daily prompt for {{ date_line | escape }}, artwork by {{ credit | escape }}"
      {%- comment -%} Storefront shows the date-selected entry only; the theme editor reveals every entry so Ryan and Gary can see and edit each day's questions. {%- endcomment -%}
      {% unless is_current %}{% unless request.design_mode %}hidden{% endunless %}{% endunless %}
      {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
    >

      <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__art{% if art_src_2 != blank %} theinmag-daily-prompt__art--pair{% endif %}">
        {%- if art_src != blank -%}
          <img
            class="theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img"
            src="{{ art_src }}"
            alt="{{ block.settings.artwork_alt | escape }}"
            width="{{ iw }}"
            height="{{ ih }}"
            {% if is_current %}loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}
            decoding="async"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if art_src_2 != blank -%}
          <img
            class="theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img"
            src="{{ art_src_2 }}"
            alt="{{ block.settings.artwork_alt | escape }}"
            width="{{ block.settings.image_w_2 | default: 1600 }}"
            height="{{ block.settings.image_h_2 | default: 1200 }}"
            {% if is_current %}loading="eager"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}
            decoding="async"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__panel">
        <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__panel-inner">

          {%- comment -%}
            Attribution + write-up sit ABOVE the eyebrow, off the image. The write-up
            is the kid's own voice (a short quote), line-clamped so a long one can
            never push the questions below the fold.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__by">
            {%- if block.settings.artwork_title != blank -%}
              <p class="theinmag-daily-prompt__art-title">{{ block.settings.artwork_title }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if credit != blank -%}
              <p class="theinmag-daily-prompt__credit-by">{{ credit }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.writeup != blank -%}
              <blockquote class="theinmag-daily-prompt__writeup" data-dp-writeup>{{ block.settings.writeup }}</blockquote>
              <button type="button" class="theinmag-daily-prompt__writeup-more" data-dp-writeup-more hidden>read more</button>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          {%- comment -%} Shuffle control: jumps to a random OTHER past entry, client-side. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__nav">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle"
              data-dp-shuffle
              {% if past_count < 1 %}disabled{% endif %}
              aria-label="Show a different past prompt"
            >
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="16 3 21 3 21 8"/><line x1="4" y1="20" x2="21" y2="3"/><polyline points="21 16 21 21 16 21"/><line x1="15" y1="15" x2="21" y2="21"/><line x1="4" y1="4" x2="9" y2="9"/></svg>
              <span>something different</span>
            </button>
            {%- comment -%} Only shown on non-current entries, so a viewer can jump back to the current day's prompt. {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- unless is_current -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="theinmag-daily-prompt__today"
                data-dp-today
                aria-label="Back to today's prompt"
              >back to today's</button>
            {%- endunless -%}
          </div>

          <p class="theinmag-daily-prompt__eyebrow">
            daily prompt
            {%- if date_line != blank -%}
              <span class="theinmag-daily-prompt__eyebrow-date">{{ date_line }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>

          {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="theinmag-daily-prompt__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            PLACEHOLDER questions. Real questions come from a pre-generate-and-human-
            approve pipeline (Yogi drafts, a human gates), which is NOT part of this
            build. Each entry carries three open, discussion-first questions that
            Ryan and Gary can see and edit here before the prompt ever displays.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <ol class="theinmag-daily-prompt__questions">
            {%- for n in (1..3) -%}
              {%- assign qkey = 'question_' | append: n -%}
              {%- assign q = block.settings[qkey] -%}
              {%- if q != blank -%}
                <li class="theinmag-daily-prompt__q">
                  <span class="theinmag-daily-prompt__q-num" aria-hidden="true">{{ n }}</span>
                  <span class="theinmag-daily-prompt__q-text">{{ q }}</span>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ol>

          {%- comment -%} The creative task: one open, imaginative invitation, bespoke to THIS creation. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if block.settings.creative_task != blank -%}
            <p class="theinmag-daily-prompt__task">
              <span class="theinmag-daily-prompt__task-label">{{ section.settings.task_label | default: 'The creative task' }}</span>
              {%- if section.settings.invite_link != blank -%}
                <a class="theinmag-daily-prompt__task-text" href="{{ section.settings.invite_link }}">{{ block.settings.creative_task }}</a>
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="theinmag-daily-prompt__task-text">{{ block.settings.creative_task }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if total == 0 -%}
    <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__empty">
      <p>Add a daily prompt entry in the theme editor to fill this page.</p>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ===== BELOW THE FOLD: the sales loop back to memberships ===== {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__loop">
    <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-inner">

      <div class="theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-head">
        <h2 class="theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-title">{{ section.settings.loop_heading }}</h2>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} A single kid character floats in the right margin, clear of the centred heading, shown only where there is room beside it (wide screens). {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-char" aria-hidden="true">
        <span data-theinmag-pool-character></span>
      </span>

      {%- comment -%}
        The three creativity tiles (competitions / live gallery / membership),
        rendered from the shared snippet so they are pixel-identical to the tiles
        on /pages/submitted. The snippet carries its own markup, CSS and gallery
        fetch, and includes theinmag-competitions-data itself. Included (not
        rendered) so it inherits this section's settings scope.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- include 'theinmag-creativity-tiles' -%}

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} Page-level JSON-LD: BreadcrumbList (always-on) + WebPage. No kid names in schema (gallery rule). {%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": {{ shop.url | json }} },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Daily prompt", "item": {{ shop.url | append: page.url | json }} }
  ]
}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "theINmag daily prompt",
  "description": "A daily classroom talking point built around one real Australian kid's creation, with open discussion questions for ages 5 to 13.",
  "url": {{ shop.url | append: page.url | json }},
  "isPartOf": { "@type": "WebSite", "name": {{ shop.name | json }}, "url": {{ shop.url | json }} }
}
</script>

<script>
  (function () {
    var section = document.querySelector('[data-theinmag-daily-prompt]');
    if (!section) return;
    if (section.__dpInit) return;
    section.__dpInit = true;

    var entries = Array.prototype.slice.call(section.querySelectorAll('[data-dp-entry]'));

    /* Write-up expand. Reveal a "read more" only when the clamped quote actually
       overflows, and toggle it open in place on click. Runs before the shuffle nav
       below so it works even with a single entry. Hidden entries have no height, so
       they are synced when shown (see show()) rather than now. */
    function syncWriteup(entry) {
      var q = entry.querySelector('[data-dp-writeup]');
      var more = entry.querySelector('[data-dp-writeup-more]');
      if (!q || !more) return;
      if (q.classList.contains('is-expanded')) { more.hidden = false; return; }
      more.hidden = (q.scrollHeight <= q.clientHeight + 2);
    }
    function collapseWriteup(entry) {
      var q = entry.querySelector('[data-dp-writeup]');
      var more = entry.querySelector('[data-dp-writeup-more]');
      if (q) { q.classList.remove('is-expanded'); }
      if (more) { more.textContent = 'read more'; }
    }
    section.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      var mb = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-dp-writeup-more]');
      if (!mb) return;
      var entry = mb.closest('[data-dp-entry]');
      var q = entry && entry.querySelector('[data-dp-writeup]');
      if (!q) return;
      mb.textContent = q.classList.toggle('is-expanded') ? 'read less' : 'read more';
    });
    /* Sync every currently-visible entry now (entry 0 on the storefront, all in the
       theme editor) and again on resize, since the clamp count shifts with width. */
    function syncVisible() {
      entries.forEach(function (entry) { if (!entry.hidden) syncWriteup(entry); });
    }
    syncVisible();
    window.addEventListener('resize', syncVisible);

    /* Date-driven roles come from the server: which entry is today's, which are the
       past pool, which are future (hidden and never revealed client-side). */
    var currentIndex = 0;
    var pastPool = [];
    entries.forEach(function (entry, i) {
      var role = entry.getAttribute('data-dp-role');
      if (role === 'current') { currentIndex = i; }
      else if (role === 'past') { pastPool.push(i); }
    });

    if (pastPool.length < 1) return; /* nothing to shuffle to: one entry stands alone */

    /* Preload the current + past-pool images so a shuffle swaps instantly, with no
       blank flash. Future entries stay lazy: they are hidden and never revealed. */
    entries.forEach(function (entry) {
      if (entry.getAttribute('data-dp-role') === 'future') { return; }
      var im = entry.querySelector('.theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img');
      if (im) { im.loading = 'eager'; }
    });

    var live = section.querySelector('[data-dp-live]');
    var current = currentIndex; /* the date-selected "today" entry */

    function announce(i) {
      if (!live) return;
      var label = entries[i].getAttribute('aria-label') || '';
      live.textContent = label;
    }

    function show(i, keepFocus) {
      if (i < 0 || i > entries.length - 1 || i === current) return;
      collapseWriteup(entries[current]);
      entries[current].hidden = true;
      entries[i].hidden = false;
      syncWriteup(entries[i]);
      current = i;
      announce(i);
      /* Keep focus inside the panel on the shuffle button of the new entry, so a
         keyboard user is not dropped to the top of the page. */
      if (keepFocus) {
        var btn = entries[i].querySelector('[data-dp-shuffle]');
        if (btn) { try { btn.focus(); } catch (e) {} }
      }
    }

    /* Pick a random entry from the PAST pool that is not the one already showing,
       then show it. Future entries are never in the pool, so a shuffle can only ever
       land on a past prompt (or stay put when the pool holds a single entry). */
    function shuffle() {
      if (pastPool.length < 1) { return; }
      var i = current;
      var guard = 0;
      while (i === current && guard < 50) {
        i = pastPool[Math.floor(Math.random() * pastPool.length)];
        guard++;
      }
      show(i, true);
    }

    /* Delegate: only the visible entry's shuffle button is reachable, so a plain
       click handler on the section routes correctly to the current entry. */
    section.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      var btn = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-dp-shuffle]');
      if (btn) { shuffle(); return; }
      /* Back to today's: jump to the date-selected current entry. The button only
         exists on non-current entries, so this is only reachable when off today. */
      var today = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-dp-today]');
      if (today) { show(currentIndex, true); }
    });

    /* Safety net: if an entry declared no width/height, refine its orientation
       from the loaded image so the layout is still right. Declared sizes win. */
    entries.forEach(function (entry) {
      if (entry.getAttribute('data-dp-orient')) return;
      var img = entry.querySelector('.theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img');
      if (!img) return;
      var apply = function () {
        if (!img.naturalWidth || !img.naturalHeight) return;
        var portrait = img.naturalHeight > img.naturalWidth;
        entry.classList.toggle('is-portrait', portrait);
        entry.classList.toggle('is-landscape', !portrait);
      };
      if (img.complete) { apply(); } else { img.addEventListener('load', apply); }
    });
  })();
</script>


{%- stylesheet -%}
  /* ================================================================
     theinmag-daily-prompt
     ================================================================ */

  .theinmag-daily-prompt {
    background-color: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA);
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__vh {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px; height: 1px;
    padding: 0; margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    white-space: nowrap; border: 0;
  }

  /* ---- Colour styles (three on-brand pairs). Panel text always inky-purple-navy,
     the universal safe text colour, so no pair-contrast rule is broken. ---- */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__hero--lavender {
    --dp-bg: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA);
    --dp-panel: var(--color-lavender, #E8DEEF);
    --dp-accent: var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A);
  }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__hero--sky {
    --dp-bg: #FDFAF5;
    --dp-panel: var(--color-sky, #C9E5E8);
    --dp-accent: var(--color-teal-dark, #2D6878);
  }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__hero--mint {
    --dp-bg: #F4ECD2;
    --dp-panel: var(--color-mint, #D6EAD9);
    --dp-accent: var(--color-sage-dark, #4A7C5C);
  }

  /* ---- Above the fold: split hero ----
     Mobile-first: the hero stacks (art on top, whole image visible, panel below).
     The desktop rules below turn it into the fluid-centreline flex row. */

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background-color: var(--dp-bg, var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA));
  }

  /* A hidden entry must leave the flow. The flex display above outranks the UA
     [hidden] rule, so state it explicitly or every entry stacks and the visible
     one is pushed below the fold. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__hero[hidden] { display: none; }

  /* ART pane: creation shown IN FULL, never cropped or distorted. On mobile the
     image is capped by height so the whole thing shows above the panel. */
  /* Ground behind the creation is the PANEL colour, not cream, so any letterbox
     space above/below a landscape image reads as one continuous field with the
     prompt panel on the right. A portrait hugs the column edge and shows none. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__art {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: clamp(16px, 5vw, 28px) clamp(14px, 5vw, 28px) 0;
    min-width: 0;
    background-color: var(--dp-panel, var(--color-lavender, #E8DEEF));
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img {
    display: block;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 48vh;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  /* Two-up: two images side by side in the art pane, each shown whole and never
     distorted. The column shrink-wraps to their combined width, so a pair reads as
     a wide (landscape) column. Each image is capped to just under half the pane. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__art--pair { gap: clamp(10px, 1.6vw, 22px); }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__art--pair .theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img { max-width: 48%; }

  /* Wide classroom display is the PRIMARY viewport: the whole split fits one
     screen with no scroll. Reserve ~132px for the sticky header + a little air,
     so the sales loop begins exactly at the fold. */
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__hero {
      flex-direction: row;
      height: calc(100vh - 132px);
      min-height: 540px;
      max-height: 900px;
    }

    /* FLUID CENTRELINE. The art column shrink-wraps to the image's own width
       (flex-basis:auto reads the image's rendered width, which is height x aspect
       once the row height is definite), so the column hugs the creation exactly and
       the image sits flush left with NO dead ground beside it. A portrait yields a
       narrow column and a wide panel (more room for the writing); a landscape yields
       a wide column and a narrower panel. Only the max is guarded: a very wide
       landscape caps at 60% so the panel keeps room. No min, so a portrait never
       leaves a strip of mismatched ground next to it. */
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__art {
      flex: 0 1 auto;
      min-width: 0;
      max-width: 60%;
      padding: 0;
      height: 100%;
    }

    /* height:100% + width:auto shows the whole image floor to ceiling, never
       cropped. max-width:100% caps a very wide landscape to the column; object-fit
       contain then letterboxes it (top/bottom ground) rather than cropping. Any
       ground revealed is the day's style ground, reading as intentional space. */
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img {
      height: 100%;
      width: auto;
      max-width: 100%;
      max-height: none;
    }

    /* In a pair, each image is bounded by height AND half-width, so both fit whole
       without either being forced to full height (which would distort it against
       the width cap). object-fit contain keeps every pixel of aspect. */
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__art--pair .theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img {
      height: auto;
      width: auto;
      max-height: 100%;
      max-width: 48%;
      object-fit: contain;
    }

    /* The panel takes ALL the space the art column leaves, right out to the
       section's right edge. Without this it defaulted to flex:0 1 auto and only
       hugged its content, so a strip of the day's ground was left down the right
       of the coloured panel (very visible on a portrait entry, where the art
       column is narrow and the leftover region is wide). flex:1 fills it, so the
       panel colour AND its text reach the viewport edge. */
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__panel {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
    }
  }

  /* Identity tile: the attribution line + the kid's write-up wrapped in a warm
     cream card that lifts off the coloured panel field, so it is the first thing
     the eye lands on. Cream is an existing brand token (never a pure-white
     field); the day's accent frames the left edge and colours the byline, tying
     the card to that day's palette. A soft shadow gives depth independent of hue
     (a deliberate colourblind-safe cue), so it reads as a card even on the
     lavender day where cream and panel are closest in tone. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__by {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(4px, 0.6vw, 7px);
    background-color: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--dp-accent, var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D));
    border-radius: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    padding: clamp(13px, 1.5vw, 18px) clamp(15px, 1.7vw, 20px);
    box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.12);
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__art-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 24px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  /* The kid's name and place: the loudest line in the card, in the day's accent
     colour (all three pass AA on cream) so the identity leads. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__credit-by {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(13px, 1.45vw, 16px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--dp-accent, var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D));
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* The kid's own words: a warm quote, not a caption. Line-clamped to 3 lines so a
     long write-up can never push the questions below the fold. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__writeup {
    margin: clamp(4px, 0.6vw, 7px) 0 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 16px);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--dp-accent, var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D));
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.55vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.42;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 3;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Expanded state: the full write-up in place. Triggered on click; on load the
     clamp holds so a long one can never push the questions below the fold. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__writeup.is-expanded {
    -webkit-line-clamp: unset;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__writeup-more {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.2vw, 14px);
    color: var(--dp-accent, var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D));
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__writeup-more:hover { opacity: 0.8; }

  /* PROMPT panel: warm coloured field, inky-purple-navy text (safe on every style). */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__panel {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px) clamp(22px, 4vw, 60px) clamp(26px, 4vw, 52px);
    min-width: 0;
    background-color: var(--dp-panel, var(--color-lavender, #E8DEEF));
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__panel-inner {
    width: 100%;
    /* Raised from 620px and left-aligned (was centred) so the lines run longer
       across the fuller panel, especially on a portrait entry where the panel is
       now wide. The panel's own padding keeps the text off the right edge. */
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(8px, 1vw, 13px);
  }

  /* ---- Shuffle control (subtle, sits at the top of the panel, adds no height
     that would push the hero below the fold) ---- */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Back to today's: a quieter text button beside the shuffle, only present once
     the viewer has moved off today. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__today {
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    padding: 7px 6px;
    color: var(--dp-accent, var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D));
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.2vw, 14px);
    line-height: 1;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__today:hover,
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__today:focus-visible { opacity: 0.75; }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 7px 15px 7px 12px;
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.28);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.2vw, 14px);
    line-height: 1;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 0.18s ease, border-color 0.18s ease, opacity 0.18s ease;
  }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle:hover,
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle:focus-visible {
    background-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.08);
    border-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.5);
    outline: none;
  }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--color-yellow, #F9C23C); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle:disabled { opacity: 0.32; cursor: default; }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle:disabled:hover { background: transparent; border-color: rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.28); }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px 14px;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(12px, 1.3vw, 14px);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__eyebrow-date {
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-transform: none;
    opacity: 0.66;
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__heading {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-synthesis: none;
    font-size: clamp(29px, 3.6vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__questions {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(11px, 1.5vw, 16px);
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__q {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 16px);
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__q-num {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: clamp(30px, 3.4vw, 38px);
    height: clamp(30px, 3.4vw, 38px);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background-color: var(--dp-accent, var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D));
    color: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA);
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.7vw, 19px);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__q-text {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(17px, 1.75vw, 22px);
    line-height: 1.38;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  /* The creative task: a small eyebrow label above one open, imaginative line. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__task {
    margin: clamp(2px, 0.8vw, 8px) 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__task-label {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(11px, 1.05vw, 12px);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dp-accent, var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A));
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__task-text {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }
  a.theinmag-daily-prompt__task-text {
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--dp-accent, var(--color-purple-dark, #5D3A7A));
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }
  a.theinmag-daily-prompt__task-text:hover,
  a.theinmag-daily-prompt__task-text:focus-visible { text-decoration-color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D); }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__empty {
    padding: clamp(40px, 8vw, 96px) 24px;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif);
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* ---- Below the fold: the sales loop ---- */

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__loop {
    background-color: var(--color-cream, #FBF6EA);
    padding: clamp(40px, 6vw, 84px) clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px) clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.08);
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-inner {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-head {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
  }

  .theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading, 'Post Regular', Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-synthesis: none;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 40px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy, #2A1F3D);
  }

  /* One kid character floats just to the right of the loop heading, level with
     it and nestled in close. The heading text is centred inside the 1180px
     inner, so anchoring the character off centre (left 50% plus a fixed offset)
     keeps a steady gap from the heading at every width above the breakpoint. It
     is hidden below that width so it can never sit over the heading on tablet or
     mobile. If a wider width ever pushes it into the heading, scale it back in a
     media query rather than letting it cover the words. */
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-char {
    position: absolute;
    top: 20px;
    left: 50%;
    margin-left: 244px;
    width: clamp(120px, 12vw, 172px);
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    display: none;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-char .theinmag-pool-character__img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  @media (min-width: 1040px) { .theinmag-daily-prompt__loop-char { display: block; } }

  /* ---- Mobile + iPad: stack creation over the prompt panel, whole image visible ---- */
  @media (max-width: 999px) {
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__art { padding: clamp(18px, 5vw, 32px) clamp(16px, 5vw, 32px) clamp(4px, 2vw, 12px); }
    /* Portrait gets more room than landscape, but both show the whole image. */
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__hero.is-portrait .theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img { max-height: 54vh; }
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__hero.is-landscape .theinmag-daily-prompt__art-img { max-height: 42vh; }
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__panel { align-items: flex-start; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-daily-prompt__shuffle { transition: none; }
  }
{%- endstylesheet -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Daily prompt",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "theinmag-daily-prompt-section",
  "max_blocks": 30,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Each daily entry is a block below, one per weekday, each with its own date. The page is DATE-DRIVEN: it shows the entry whose date is today (or the most recent past date when today has none), earlier dates become the 'something different' pool, and future-dated entries stay hidden until their day. Block order does not matter. To add a new day, add a block and set its date."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Lead-in + creative task (shared label + link)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Lead-in heading", "default": "Let's talk about this creation." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "task_label", "label": "Creative task label", "default": "The creative task" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "invite_link", "label": "Creative task link", "default": "/pages/send-in" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The loop back (below the fold)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "loop_heading", "label": "Loop heading", "default": "Keep the creativity going" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Competitions tile (live logos)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "comps_name", "label": "Competitions card name", "default": "Competitions" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "comps_link", "label": "Competitions card link", "default": "/pages/competitions" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "comps_count", "label": "How many live comps", "min": 3, "max": 8, "step": 1, "default": 4 },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Live gallery tile (real creations)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "gallery_name", "label": "Gallery card name", "default": "Live gallery" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "gallery_link", "label": "Gallery card link", "default": "/pages/gallery" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "gallery_count", "label": "How many creations", "min": 4, "max": 14, "step": 1, "default": 10 },
    { "type": "text", "id": "gallery_feed_url", "label": "Gallery feed URL (advanced)", "default": "https://theinmag-gallery-review.heyhey-53f.workers.dev/gallery-data.json" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Membership tile (emphasised)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_name", "label": "Membership card name", "default": "Membership" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_headline", "label": "Membership money tile", "default": "Grab a membership from $28.90" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_blurb", "label": "Membership card blurb (optional)", "default": "Posted three times a year, ad-free and made by kids." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_cta_label", "label": "Membership CTA label", "default": "Grab a membership" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_link", "label": "Membership card link", "default": "/products/membership" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "membership_image", "label": "Membership image" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_image_fallback", "label": "Fallback image filename (theme asset)", "default": "product-membership.jpg" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_image_alt", "label": "Membership image alt text", "default": "A theINmag membership, posted to your door" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "membership_hover", "label": "Membership hover image" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_hover_fallback", "label": "Fallback hover image filename (theme asset)", "default": "product-membership-hover.jpg" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_feature_1", "label": "Feature 1", "default": "Every issue posted to your door" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_feature_2", "label": "Feature 2", "default": "Made by kids, always ad-free" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_feature_3", "label": "Feature 3", "default": "Your creations could be published" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "membership_feature_4", "label": "Feature 4", "default": "Pause or cancel anytime" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "membership_review_count", "label": "How many reviews to show", "min": 0, "max": 4, "step": 1, "default": 2 }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "entry",
      "name": "Daily entry",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "One weekday's prompt. Give it a date; the page selects the right day automatically and it joins the past pool afterwards. Questions are human-checked data: a human sees and edits every one here before it ever shows. No live generation. Keep them simple, universal and open, so they work for any creation and a teacher can run a rich open task off them: notice, wonder, what happens next."
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "date", "label": "Date (YYYY-MM-DD)", "info": "Used for the date line and, on auto style, to pick the colour.", "default": "2026-09-14" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Creation image" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "image_url", "label": "Creation image URL", "info": "Used when no image is picked. Paste a moderated gallery image." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "image_asset", "label": "Creation image asset filename", "info": "Optional. A file in the theme's /assets/ (e.g. a pre-rotated image). Resolved via asset_url and wins over the URL above." },
        { "type": "number", "id": "image_w", "label": "Image width (px)", "info": "Sets orientation: taller than wide = portrait layout. For a pre-rotated image, use the ROTATED dimensions.", "default": 1600 },
        { "type": "number", "id": "image_h", "label": "Image height (px)", "default": 1200 },
        { "type": "text", "id": "artwork_alt", "label": "Image alt text" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "image_url_2", "label": "Second image URL (optional)", "info": "When set, both images show side by side as a clean two-up." },
        { "type": "number", "id": "image_w_2", "label": "Second image width (px)" },
        { "type": "number", "id": "image_h_2", "label": "Second image height (px)" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "artwork_title", "label": "Creation title (optional)" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "writeup", "label": "Kid's write-up (their own words)", "info": "Shown in the panel as the child's voice. Clamped to three lines on the page." },
        {
          "type": "select",
